      "writtenOn": "2022-04-01T16:22:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I convinced myself that SkShaper is doing the right thing in this case: it preserves whitespace before line breaks (at the end of the first line, next line starts with a non-whitespace char).\n\nAE does the same thing: trailing whitespace before line break is still there, it\u0027s just being ignored for alignment.  E.g. it extends outside the paragraph box with right-align, you can move the cursor through it, and it participates in character-based range selectors (for text animators).\n\nSo it would be incorrect/noticeable to trim, as I was thinking initially -- it\u0027s only alignment, which is handled outside SkShaper.",
      "parentUuid": "af3b9bb6_c481aa7b",
      "revId": "78fbc665d123652aae4eaefb3ddc6b1377182a0b",
